from __future__ import annotations

NAME = "Enceladus, the Geyser Moon"
AMBIENCE = "Singing Bowl"

# A soothing sleep-lecture about a tiny white moon whose icy fountains feed Saturn's E ring from a warm hidden sea.
SECTIONS = [['You have nowhere to be right now.', 'There is nothing left to do, and nothing left to fix.', 'Let your body grow heavy, sinking softly into the place where you are resting.', 'Feel the weight of your shoulders letting go, melting downward.', 'Let your jaw soften, and the small muscles around your eyes grow still.', 'Breathe in slowly, gently, and let the breath out even more slowly.', 'With each breath out, you sink a little deeper into stillness.', 'There is no hurry here, and no need to hold on to anything at all.', 'Let your thoughts drift loose, like soft snow falling somewhere far away.', 'And as you breathe, imagine yourself growing light, lighter than air, beginning to float.', 'You drift gently upward and outward, into a quiet velvet dark, toward a tiny brilliant white moon glittering near the great ringed planet.', 'You float toward it slowly, peacefully, with all the time in the world.'], ['Ahead of you, that little white moon grows softly nearer.', 'It is called Enceladus, a small moon that circles the planet Saturn.', 'It is a tiny world, only about five hundred kilometres across.', 'That is small enough to nestle inside a single country, with room to spare.', 'Long ago, in the year seventeen eighty nine, an astronomer named William Herschel first saw it through his telescope.', 'He saw only a faint point of light, a small spark beside the rings.', 'For a long time after that, it stayed a quiet mystery, far away in the dark.', 'And now you drift toward it gently, the way snow drifts down to the ground.', 'It glows ahead of you, white and clean and calm.', 'There is no rush in this place, and no sound at all.', 'You simply float closer, breathing slow and easy.', 'Let the little moon draw you softly nearer.'], ['As you come closer, you see how astonishingly white this little moon is.', 'Its whole surface is fresh, clean ice, smooth and bright.', 'It is one of the whitest, most reflective objects in the entire solar system.', 'Almost all the sunlight that touches it bounces straight back into space.', 'Because it keeps so little of that warmth, the surface is very, very cold.', 'It is like a perfect field of new fallen snow, untouched and gleaming.', 'Imagine the soft white glow of it spreading out beneath you.', 'The light is gentle here, pale and silvery and kind.', 'You float above a world of quiet, shining frost.', 'No footprints mark it, and no wind disturbs it.', 'It is simply still, and silent, and luminous.', 'You breathe in slowly, and let the brightness soothe you.'], ['Now you drift gently down toward the south of this little moon.', 'Here, across the bottom of the world, run four long cracks in the ice.', 'People have given them a soft, friendly name, the tiger stripes.', 'These cracks are a little warmer than the cold ice around them.', 'And from these warm cracks, something quiet and wonderful rises.', 'Tall fountains of water ice and vapour drift silently up into space.', 'They are geysers, gentle plumes climbing hundreds of kilometres high.', 'They make no sound at all, these towering silver fountains.', 'Tiny crystals of ice glitter in the sunlight as they rise.', 'They look like slow, shimmering veils, sparkling against the dark.', 'You watch them lift and spread, calm and endless and bright.', 'And you wonder softly where all this water could be coming from.'], ['The answer is hidden, and it is beautiful.', 'Far beneath the icy shell of this little moon lies an ocean.', 'It is a whole sea of liquid salty water, wrapped all the way around the world.', 'It hides quietly under kilometres of ice, dark and deep and warm.', 'You might wonder how an ocean could stay warm so far from the sun.', 'The great planet Saturn squeezes and stretches this little moon as it circles by.', 'That gentle, endless flexing makes a soft warmth deep inside.', 'And so, beneath the frozen surface, a secret sea stays liquid and alive.', 'From that warm ocean, the fountains rise, feeding the silver plumes above.', 'Imagine it, a hidden warm sea beneath a quiet field of ice.', 'A secret kept safe and gentle in the cold and the dark.', 'You breathe slowly, holding that warm quiet thought.'], ['A spacecraft once came here, a gentle traveller named Cassini.', 'It flew right through the tall fountains of ice, very softly.', 'It tasted what the plumes were made of as it drifted through.', 'It found water, and salts, and the small molecules that life is built upon.', 'There were even hints of warm vents far down on the ocean floor.', 'All the gentle ingredients for life, mixed in that hidden sea.', 'No one knows if anything lives there, in the warm dark water below.', 'It is a soft and hopeful wonder, a question to hold lightly.', 'Could a tiny world like this cradle a secret of its own?', 'Meanwhile, the finest ice grains drift far out from the fountains.', 'They spread into a wide, faint ring that circles Saturn, called the E ring.', 'You float among that gentle haze of glittering snow, calm and at peace.'], ['Now let the little moon grow soft and distant once more.', 'The silent fountains of ice still rise, slow and shimmering and white.', 'And the finest crystals begin, ever so gently, to drift back down.', 'They settle like snow, soft and slow and weightless.', 'Down they sink, quiet and bright, coming to rest.', 'Feel yourself settling too, drifting softly downward into your bed.', 'Heavier now, and warmer, and wonderfully calm.', 'The fountains grow still, and the white moon grows dim and far.', 'Let every last thought drift down like falling snow and come to rest.', 'There is nothing to hold, and nowhere to go, only this quiet.', 'Breathe out slowly, and let yourself sink all the way into sleep.', 'Rest now, soft and still, beneath a gentle fall of silver snow.']]
